<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka's Jan trade gap rises 4.2 percent.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka's Jan trade gap rises 4.2 percent.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's trade gap for January rose 4.2 percent to $154 million over the same period last year, the Central Bank said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It said the trade gap in January 1996 was $148 million.</p>
<p>Exports in January this year were $320 million while imports in the same month were pegged at $474 million, the Central Bank said.</p>
</text>
